course: dictionary
lesson: 3030
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word ear can mean a part of your body, the ability to hear, or the top part of a cereal plant. Which meaning is right depends on the words around it, so read the whole sentence before you choose.
explain: «She has a good ear for music.» Here ear is not a body part. The words good and music show it means being able to hear and notice sounds well. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: Some words belong to set phrases, which have their own meaning. «All ears» means listening carefully, and «play it by ear» means deciding as you go. You cannot work these out word by word, so learn the whole phrase.
fact: Ear means one of the two parts on the sides of the head that you hear with.
fact: Ear can also mean the ability to hear or notice sounds, as in «a good ear for music».
fact: Ear can mean the top part of a cereal plant that holds the grains, as in «an ear of corn».
fact: «All ears» means listening carefully, and «play it by ear» means deciding as you go.
fact: Never put things in your ears, because loud noise can damage hearing.
exercise: «The fennec fox has huge ears that give off heat.» What are the ears in this sentence? | The top part of a cereal plant | A kind of loud noise | *Parts on the sides of the head that you hear with | The ability to notice sounds
exercise: «She has a good ear for music.» What does ear mean here? | A part of the head | *The ability to hear and notice sounds | The top part of a plant | A ring worn on the lobe
exercise: Which meaning fits «an ear of corn»? | Being good at listening to music | Part of the head you hear with | *The top part of a cereal plant that holds the grains | Listening carefully to a teacher
test: Which meaning of «all ears» is right when someone says, «I am all ears»? | Hungry for food | *Listening carefully | Angry about the noise | Tired and ready for bed
test: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears.» What may the spots help cubs do? | *Follow their mother | Sleep through the day | Grow longer legs | Swim faster
exam: «An elephant flaps its huge ears to cool its blood.» Which meaning of ears is used here? | The top part of a cereal plant | Loud noises that can damage hearing | *Parts on the sides of the head | The ability to notice sounds
